    <string name="help_section_intro">Welcome to the Te Papa Collections app, where
        you can explore &amp; discover the many wonders of the Museum of New
        Zealand, Te Papa Tongarewa, located in Cable Street, Wellington. Within the
        different sections of this app, you can search the different sections of the
        museum. You can search by type (14 in all), or by collection: whether that\'s
        an object (9 collections) or a specimen (13 collections). Check out the
        three-dot menu at top right to see a sample of each type/collection.</string>
    <string name="help_section_options"><![CDATA[In each of the sections, although
        the actual results will differ, the methods of searching are the same. Use
        the <B>Manage Search</B> icon (an example of which is shown on each search
        page) to choose either your preferred type or collection, and/or to focus
        the query by specifying exact match, any word, all words, etc.]]></string>
    <string name="help_section_faves"><![CDATA[If you add a search result as a
        favourite, it will show up in the <B>Your Favourites</B> section of
        the app. The absolute <I>minimum</I> of information, including a
        direct link to that record, is saved locally to enable retrieval of
        the item. When reviewing a favourite, the item is redownloaded for
        display. Favourites can be sorted by date added, by name, or by type.
        You can remove favourites either singularly, by using the Remove Favourite
        icon next to each fave, or you can remove <I>all</I> favourites by
        accessing the three-dot menu in the Your Favourites section.]]></string>
    <string name="help_section_settings_1"><![CDATA[In the <B>Settings</B> section
        of the app, you can specify the number of results to retrieve each time. If
        there are <I>more</I> results than this number available, you can download
        these \"on the fly\" if desired. There\'s the option to save <I>successful</I>
        queries to the app database on your device, for future use. For privacy
        reasons, this setting is <I>not</I> enabled by default. These queries
        can be cleared at any time from the three-dot menu in Settings.]]></string>
    <string name="help_section_settings_2"><![CDATA[Also in Settings is the option to
        save the <B>time &amp; date</B> when adding an item to your favourites. This
        timestamp will show at the bottom of each listing in your favourites list, if
        enabled. You also have a setting to show a Hybrid/<B>Satellite</B> map-type
        when viewing Places on the map. One <I>final</I> setting enables viewing full
        screen images at their maximum bounds, meaning that you can then \"scroll\"
        the image either left/right or up/down to view it in its entirety.]]></string>

